-# The SigNoz k8s-infra agent (platform/observability/k8s-infra.yaml, crew#388) reads container
-# logs from /var/log/pods and node metrics from the host filesystem. That is the whole job of a
-# node agent, and it cannot be done without hostPath volumes, which disallow-host-path and
-# restrict-volume-types refuse by design. The waiver is scoped to the one DaemonSet and those
-# two policies; the otel-deployment Deployment next to it passes the full restricted profile.
-# Only the policies bin/idp-kyverno-render shows failing are listed; the incident test refuses
-# a waiver for a policy the chart already passes. It lives in platform/edge because Kyverno
-# honours exceptions from namespace kyverno only (crew#325) and this directory has no
-# namespace transformer. The DaemonSet lives in observability-agent (the HelmRelease's
-# targetNamespace), whose PSA label admits hostPath; see platform/observability/platform/edge/k8s-infra-namespace.yaml.
-apiVersion: kyverno.io/v2
-kind: PolicyException
-metadata:
-  name: k8s-infra-node-agent
-  namespace: kyverno
-spec:
-  exceptions:
-    - policyName: disallow-host-path
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: restrict-volume-types
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-  match:
-    any:
-      - resources:
-          kinds: [DaemonSet, Pod]
-          namespaces: [observability-agent]
-          # the release is observability-agent-k8s-infra (helm-controller: <targetNamespace>-<name>), crew#483
-          names: [observability-agent-k8s-infra-otel-agent*]
diff --git a/platform/edge/k8s-infra-namespace.yaml b/platform/edge/k8s-infra-namespace.yaml
deleted file mode 100644
index ed7b0d6b2..000000000
--- a/platform/edge/k8s-infra-namespace.yaml
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,22 +0,0 @@
-# The node agent's own namespace (crew#388, 2026-08-27). It lives in edge, next to the Kyverno
-# exception for the same DaemonSet, because platform/observability/kustomization.yaml sets
-# namespace: observability and that transformer renames every Namespace object it sees. Measured in cluster-state events_warning:
-#   Error creating: pods "k8s-infra-otel-agent-q6z9l" is forbidden: violates PodSecurity
-#   "restricted:latest": restricted volume types (volumes "varlog", "varlibdockercontainers",
-#   "hostfs" use restricted volume type "hostPath")
-# The refusal came from the Pod Security Admission label on namespace observability, not from
-# Kyverno. platform/edge/k8s-infra-exception.yaml waives the Kyverno rules, and a Kyverno
-# exception cannot waive a PSA label: PSA is enforced by the API server per namespace, and both
-# restricted and baseline forbid hostPath. A node agent that reads /var/log/pods and the host
-# filesystem therefore needs a namespace whose enforce level is privileged. Giving that level to
-# observability would also lift it for SigNoz, ClickHouse and Langfuse, so the agent gets its own
-# namespace and observability stays restricted. warn and audit stay restricted here so any other
-# workload that lands in this namespace is reported.
-apiVersion: v1
-kind: Namespace
-metadata:
-  name: observability-agent
-  labels:
-    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: privileged
-    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted
-    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted
